+## Usage `afterModelResponse` reports
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message, after the round loop exits, and the usage it is handed is the sum of every provider call in the turn — a turn driven through two tool rounds reports all three calls' tokens, so a deployer billing or auditing from the hook counts the expensive turns in full rather than only their last leg ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call in a turn driven through two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L68)).
+- A round whose provider reported no usage contributes nothing to that sum rather than undefining it: the rounds that did report are still counted ([validated by: still totals the rounds that reported when a round reports no usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
+- A turn with no tool calls reports what its single provider call reported, so the common path does not move ([validated by: reports a turn with no tool calls exactly as the single provider call reported it](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+- A turn where no round reported usage still reports nothing ([validated by: reports nothing when no round in the turn reported usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L108)).
+
